ABSTRACT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This paper establishes the D_4 representation theory of the 14-mode multiplet
at the self-paired eigenvalue lambda = 4 of the discrete 5-point Laplacian on
the periodic 8x8 torus Lambda = Z_8 x Z_8. We derive the 14-dimensional real
mode basis, the D_4 action as a signed permutation representation with
character chi_14 = (14,2,0,2,2), the orbit decomposition into three orbits of
sizes (2,8,4) with stabilizer orders (4,1,2), the irreducible decomposition
14 = 3A_1 + A_2 + 2B_1 + 2B_2 + 3E, and the isomorphism between the real mode
representation and the momentum-label permutation module.

We then derive the n_1-parity operator D = diag((-1)^(n_1^(i))) on the
multiplet as the indicator of the middle D_4 orbit. Specifically, D = +1 on
O_0 + O_2 = {nu, e, t, W, Z, H} and D = -1 on O_1 = {u, d, s, mu, dark, c, tau, b}.
This follows from the parity constraint n_1 = n_2 (mod 2) that holds on every
mode at lambda = 4.

The present revision closes the previously disclosed input P8 by deriving the
processor T = I - P_C and the class partition C = {dark, W, Z, H} from the
winding generator H_wind = i sin(pi M / 8) and the fermion/boson homogeneity
constraint. The derivation chain is

    lattice primitive -> H_wind -> {A,B,C} -> T = I - P_C,

with the winding class partition uniquely forced by requiring each class to be
fermion/boson homogeneous. This eliminates the last disclosed input in HCSM-05's
scope.

We further derive the exact closed forms in Q(sqrt(2)) for the three
independent zero-state amplitudes a_2, a_4, a_6 of HCSM-22, from the
reconstructible columns of the measurement matrix. These exact forms agree with
the HCSM-22 numerical values to all 15 printed digits. The spectral content of
the multiplet (support classes, IPRs, entropy classes) is established in
HCSM-04 and is cited. All numerical claims are verified at machine precision.

