2. SETUP
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

2.1 The substrate

The substrate is the periodic square lattice Lambda = Z_8 x Z_8 with N = 64
sites. Site (x_1, x_2) is identified with (x_1+8, x_2) and with (x_1, x_2+8).

2.2 The 5-point Laplacian

The scalar 5-point Laplacian is

    (Delta f)(x_1, x_2) = 4 f(x_1, x_2) - f(x_1+1, x_2) - f(x_1-1, x_2)
                          - f(x_1, x_2+1) - f(x_1, x_2-1).

Its eigenvalue on the complex plane wave phi_{n_1,n_2}(x_1,x_2) =
exp(2 pi i (n_1 x_1 + n_2 x_2) / 8) is

    lambda(n_1, n_2) = 4 - 2 cos(pi n_1 / 4) - 2 cos(pi n_2 / 4),
    (n_1, n_2) in {0,...,7}^2.

The self-paired eigenvalue at lambda = 4 is the unique fixed point of the
mirror symmetry lambda <-> 8 - lambda with multiplicity 2(L-1) = 14 at L = 8
(HCSM-04, Theorem 3.2).

2.3 The 14 momenta

The 14 momenta satisfying cos(pi n_1 / 4) + cos(pi n_2 / 4) = 0 are
(HCSM-04, Theorem 4.1)

    O_0 = {(0,4), (4,0)},
    O_1 = {(1,3), (1,5), (3,1), (3,7), (5,1), (5,7), (7,3), (7,5)},
    O_2 = {(2,2), (2,6), (6,2), (6,6)}.

2.4 The D_4 action

The D_4 point group of the square acts on momentum labels by

    r: (n_1, n_2) -> (-n_2, n_1) mod 8,
    s: (n_1, n_2) -> (n_1, -n_2) mod 8,

with presentation r^4 = s^2 = (rs)^2 = e. The group is
D_4 = {e, r, r^2, r^3, s, rs, r^2 s, r^3 s}, of order 8.

