4. THE D_4 ACTION AND CHARACTER
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

4.1 Action rule

For g in D_4, the action on functions is (R_g phi)(x) = phi(g^{-1} x). Direct
computation gives

    R_r C_n = C_{r(n)}, R_r S_n = S_{r(n)},
    R_s C_n = C_{s(n)}, R_s S_n = S_{s(n)}.

The representation is therefore a signed permutation on the 14-dimensional
real mode space.

4.2 Character

Theorem 4.1 (D_4 character of the real mode representation). The character of
the real mode representation on the five conjugacy classes (e, r^2, r, s, rs)
is

    chi_14 = (14, 2, 0, 2, 2).

Proof. Let P_g be the permutation matrix of g on the 14 mode labels. The
character is tr(P_g).

  Identity e. All 14 modes fixed. chi(e) = 14.

  Rotation r. A mode is fixed by r iff its momentum satisfies r(n) = n, i.e.,
  n_1 = -n_2 and n_2 = n_1, i.e., n_1 = n_2 in {0,4}. Neither (0,0) nor (4,4)
  is in the multiplet. So no mode is fixed. chi(r) = 0.

  Rotation r^2. r^2(n) = -n. Every cosine satisfies C_{-n} = C_n, so all 8
  cosine modes are fixed with epsilon = +1. Every sine satisfies
  S_{-n} = -S_n, giving diagonal entry -1 for each of the 6 sine modes.
  Character: 8*(+1) + 6*(-1) = 2. chi(r^2) = 2.

  Reflection s. s(n) = (n_1, -n_2). Fixed modes satisfy n_2 in {0,4}. Among the
  14 momenta, only (0,4) and (4,0) have n_2 in {0,4}, and both are
  self-conjugate cosines. Each contributes +1. chi(s) = 2.

  Reflection rs. rs(n) = (n_2, n_1). Fixed modes satisfy n_1 = n_2. The
  diagonal momenta in the multiplet are (2,2) and (6,6), which form one
  conjugate pair. On this pair, C_{(2,2)} -> C_{(2,2)} with epsilon = +1 and
  S_{(2,2)} -> S_{(2,2)} with epsilon = +1. The other pair {(2,6),(6,2)}
  satisfies rs(2,6) = (6,2) = -(2,6), so C_{(2,6)} -> C_{(2,6)} with
  epsilon = +1 and S_{(2,6)} -> S_{(6,2)} = -S_{(2,6)} with epsilon = -1.
  Total character on rs: (+1) + (+1) + (+1) + (-1) = 2. chi(rs) = 2. []

4.3 Isomorphism with the momentum-label module

Corollary 4.2 (Isomorphism). The real mode representation of D_4 is
isomorphic to the permutation representation on the 14 momentum labels.

Proof. Two complex representations of a finite group are isomorphic iff their
characters coincide on every conjugacy class. The momentum-label permutation
module has character (14,2,0,2,2) (HCSM-02, Sec. 7.2), matching Theorem 4.1. []

