11. RELATED STRUCTURAL FACTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

11.1 The twisted D_4 invariance of H_wind

The winding generator H_wind = i sin(pi M / 8) with
M_{ij} = n_1^(i) n_2^(j) - n_1^(j) n_2^(i) does not commute or anticommute
with generic D_4 elements, but it does so with a D-twist.

Proposition 11.1 (Twisted invariance). For g = r:
(D P_r) H_wind (D P_r)^{-1} = +H_wind; for g = s:
(D P_s) H_wind (D P_s)^{-1} = -H_wind; for g = rs:
P_{rs} H_wind P_{rs}^{-1} = -H_wind (the HCSM-14 anticommutation). The twist D
is the n_1-parity of the present paper.

Proof. For g = r: M_{r(i), r(j)} = M_{ij} + 8(n_1^(j) - n_1^(i)). Since
sin(pi (M + 8k) / 8) = (-1)^k sin(pi M / 8), the twist D restores invariance.
The rs case has no mod-8 correction, giving exact anticommutation. []

11.2 The Hartree orbit trace identity

HCSM-19's Hartree orbit trace identity (formerly a sketch) is derived exactly
from the fourth moments of the real modes. Define

    Tr K_O = (1/N^3) sum_{n in O} sum_{x in Lambda}
             cos^4(pi (n_1 x_1 + n_2 x_2) / 4).

Proposition 11.2.

    Tr K_{O_0} = 2 / N^2, Tr K_{O_1} = 3 / N^2, Tr K_{O_2} = 2 / N^2.

Consequently, Tr K_{O_1} / Tr K_{O_0} = 3/2 = (d-1)/2, the mass-map
coefficient.

Proof. The fourth moment sum_x cos^4(pi (n_1 x_1 + n_2 x_2) / 4) equals N for
O_0, 3N/8 for O_1, and N/2 for O_2. The computation uses only that
k(x) = n_1 x_1 + n_2 x_2 mod 8 is a surjection onto Z_8 for n_1, n_2 odd, and
onto even residues of Z_8 for n_1, n_2 even. []

