14. CONCLUSION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This paper has established the D_4 representation theory of the 14-mode
multiplet at lambda = 4 on the periodic 8x8 torus. The 14-dimensional real
eigenspace admits an explicit orthonormal basis of two self-conjugate cosine
modes and six cosine-sine pairs. The D_4 action is a signed permutation with
character chi_14 = (14,2,0,2,2). The mode multiplet decomposes into three
orbits of sizes (2,8,4) with stabilizer orders (4,1,2). As a D_4
representation it decomposes as 3A_1 + A_2 + 2B_1 + 2B_2 + 3E.

The central result of the revised paper is that the processor T and the class
partition C = {dark, W, Z, H} are derived from the winding generator H_wind
and the fermion/boson homogeneity constraint. The derivation chain is

    lattice primitive -> H_wind -> {A,B,C} -> T = I - P_C.

The previously disclosed input (P8) is closed.

The n_1-parity operator D = diag((-1)^(n_1^(i))) is the indicator of the
middle D_4 orbit. It is D_4-invariant, commutes with the orientation flip F
(HCSM-43), and commutes with the derived processor T. Its joint spectrum with
T is the winding class partition {A,B,C}.

We also derive the exact closed forms in Q(sqrt(2)) for the three independent
zero-state amplitudes a_2, a_4, a_6 of HCSM-22, from the three reconstructible
columns of the measurement matrix. The exact forms agree with the HCSM-22
numerical values to all 15 printed digits. This closes the previous open item.

The identification of the 14 modes with one Standard Model generation is a
disclosed input (HCSM-23). The spectral content of the multiplet (support
classes, IPRs, entropy classes) is established in HCSM-04 and cited.

HCSM-05 is fully derived in its own scope. All theorems of this paper are
derived from the substrate, with the processor T derived from the winding
generator H_wind and fermion/boson homogeneity. No disclosed inputs remain in
HCSM-05's own scope.

Physics is what the machine cannot cancel. The Hodge complex is the machine.
The class partition is what the machine sorts.

