APPENDIX A. EXPLICIT FORM OF THE WINDING GENERATOR
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The winding matrix M has even-integer entries. The winding generator
H_wind = i sin(pi M / 8) is Hermitian with entries in Q(sqrt(2)). Its
characteristic polynomial is

    p(lambda) = lambda^10 (lambda^2 - 8)(lambda^2 - 32).

The spectrum is {-4 sqrt(2), -2 sqrt(2), 0^(10), +2 sqrt(2), +4 sqrt(2)}.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
APPENDIX B. DERIVATION OF THE CLASS PARTITION FROM H_WIND AND HOMOGENEITY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The class partition {A, B, C} is uniquely forced by requiring each class to be
fermion/boson homogeneous and to agree with the D_4 orbit partition on 12 of
14 modes (HCSM-28, Theorem 3.1). The unique two-mode swap is {t, dark}. The
bosonic class is C = B_bos = {dark, W, Z, H}; the fermionic classes are
A = {nu, e, t} and B = {u, d, s, mu, c, tau, b}.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
APPENDIX C. THE PROCESSOR T
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The processor T = I - P_C is the rank-10 orthogonal projection with
im(T) = A + B = F and ker(T) = C = B_bos. In the standard mode order,

    diag(T) = (1,1,1,1,1,1,0,1,1,1,0,0,0,1).

